  "fceContents": {
    "welcome": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Welcome to the business permit demo\n\nThis playbook walks through a fictional business-registration application. You'll choose an entity type, fill in details, submit, and either receive a follow-up request or a direct decision.\n\n## What you'll see\n\n- A **draft → in progress → awaiting → requires attention → completed** status trajectory\n- A **branching path** at stage 1 (sole proprietorship vs limited company vs other)\n- **Transmissions** of types `Information`, `Submission`, `Request`, `Acceptance`, `Decision`\n- **Activities** logged at key transitions\n- **Front-channel embeds** like this one, each named and resolved via the playbook's state id\n\nClick **Start application** below to begin."
    },
    "biz-types": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Choose entity type\n\nPick the one that fits your situation. You can change later by clicking **Change business type** on the next screen.\n\n| Type | Best for | Setup time |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Sole proprietorship** | One owner, low risk, simple bookkeeping | Same day |\n| **Limited company** | Multiple founders, capital, liability protection | 2–3 weeks |\n| **Other** | Cooperative, foundation, NGO, association | Case-by-case |\n\nNot sure? Pick *Other* and a case worker will help."
    },
    "soleprop-form": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Sole proprietorship details\n\nIn a real application this view would be an actual form. For the demo we'll just describe what we'd ask for.\n\n## Required fields\n\n- **Personal ID number** (national identity number)\n- **Trade name** — must include your surname\n- **Planned start date**\n- **NACE / industry code**\n- **Estimated annual turnover** (used to determine VAT registration)\n- **Registered address**\n\n## Optional\n\n- Bookkeeping software you'll use\n- Whether you'll have any employees in year one"
    },
    "soleprop-tax": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Tax registration — sole proprietorship\n\n## VAT (mva)\n\nYou'll be auto-registered for VAT once your **12-month turnover crosses NOK 50,000**. Until then you neither charge nor reclaim VAT.\n\n## Income tax\n\nProfits are taxed as personal income at marginal rates. You'll get a pre-filled tax form each March based on what you report.\n\n## Reporting deadlines\n\n- VAT (once registered): bi-monthly\n- Annual income statement: April 30\n\nYou'll find templates in Altinn once your business number is issued."
    },
    "ltdco-form": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Limited company details\n\nIn a real application this view would be the company-formation form. For the demo, here's what we'd ask for.\n\n## Required\n\n- **Company name** — must be unique and end with `AS` (or equivalent)\n- **Articles of association** — PDF upload\n- **Share capital** — minimum NOK 30,000\n- **Founders** — names and ID numbers\n- **Board members** — chair and at least one regular member\n- **Registered office** — Norwegian address\n- **Auditor** (or declaration of exemption if eligible)\n\n## You'll upload at review\n\n- Founding meeting minutes\n- Bank confirmation of share capital deposit"
    },
    "ltdco-board": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Board documentation requirements\n\n## Founding meeting minutes\n\nThe minutes must include:\n\n- Date, time, location\n- Founders present\n- Decision to form the company\n- Adoption of articles of association\n- Election of board members\n- Decision on share capital and how it's paid\n\n## Format\n\nSigned PDF, max 10 MB. Multi-page is fine.\n\n## Bank confirmation\n\nA signed letter from the bank confirming the share capital is deposited in an account in the company's name."
    },
    "other-contact": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Other business types\n\nCooperatives, foundations, religious bodies, and NGOs each have their own paths — too varied for a self-service form.\n\n## What happens next\n\n1. **Email** us at `business-help@example.org` with a short description (2–3 paragraphs) of your structure and purpose.\n2. A case worker will **respond within 3 business days** with a tailored checklist.\n3. Once the checklist is complete you'll come back here, click **I've made contact — continue**, and we'll route the rest through this dialog."
    },
    "review": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Review summary\n\n## What we have\n\n*(In a real application, this would be a read-only render of everything filled in so far.)*\n\n- Entity type\n- Trade name / company name\n- Founders / sole proprietor\n- Address\n- Industry code\n- Tax / VAT election\n- Attached documents (if any)\n\n## Before you submit\n\n- Submission locks the application — edits afterward require contacting the case worker.\n- You'll get a receipt with a reference number you can use in any correspondence.\n- A case worker may come back with follow-up questions — you'll see them in this dialog."
    },
    "receipt": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Status: in queue\n\nYour application is **REF-2026-3142**. Estimated processing time **5–7 business days**.\n\n## What happens now\n\n1. A case worker picks up your application from the queue\n2. They review the docs and either approve or ask for more\n3. You'll see any follow-up requests as a **transmission** in this dialog\n4. You'll get the final decision via a **Decision** transmission and the dialog will move to **Completed**\n\n*This is a demo, so to keep things fast you can simulate either branch using the buttons below.*"
    },
    "receipt-tx": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Receipt — REF-2026-3142\n\n**Received** 2026-06-06 at 14:22 (UTC)\n\n**From** Trade register service desk\n**To** Applicant\n\n## Contents\n\n- Application form\n- Attachments (none required for sole prop; otherwise see below)\n- Tax registration election\n\n## Keep this reference handy\n\nUse `REF-2026-3142` when contacting us about this application. It's also stored in your transmission history above."
    },
    "docs-needed": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Documents needed\n\nThe case worker has reviewed your application and needs a couple more things.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] **Proof of address** — utility bill or bank statement, less than 3 months old\n- [ ] **Articles of association** — signed PDF (only if you formed a limited company)\n- [ ] **ID document** — passport or national ID, front page\n\nUpload each as a separate file. Max 10 MB each.\n\n## Deadline\n\n**14 days** from when you received this request. If we don't hear back the application is automatically rejected and you'll need to start over.\n\nClick **Send additional docs** below to simulate uploading."
    },
    "docs-request": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Request from case worker\n\nHi,\n\nI'm reviewing your business permit application and need a few extra documents to verify your identity and confirm the company structure. The full list is on the main view.\n\nA few notes:\n\n- The **address proof** doesn't have to be in your name if you can show a letter from the household head confirming you live there.\n- For the **articles of association** I just need the signed final version — drafts aren't enough.\n- The **ID document** should be valid (not expired).\n\nReply by attaching the documents at the bottom of this dialog. Aim for within 14 days so we don't have to close the application.\n\n— Case worker"
    },
    "final-review": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Final review\n\nYour additional documents have been received and the case worker is now finalising the decision.\n\n## What we're checking\n\n- Document authenticity (we cross-check the address proof and ID against population register data)\n- Articles of association — consistency with the form data you submitted\n- No conflicting registrations\n\n## Timing\n\nMost final reviews complete within **2 business days**. You'll get a `Decision` transmission and the dialog status moves to **Completed**."
    },
    "docs-received-tx": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Documents received\n\nAll requested documents have been received and look complete. Thanks for the quick turnaround.\n\nWe're moving the application to final review. Expect a decision within **2 business days**.\n\nNo action required from you."
    },
    "decision": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Decision: Approved\n\nYour business is now registered.\n\n## Key details\n\n- **Permit number** `BP-2026-77231`\n- **Effective date** 2026-06-15\n- **Tax registration** enabled\n- **Registry status** Active\n\nThe formal decision document is attached as a transmission below. Save it for your records — banks and insurance providers will ask to see it.\n\n## Next steps\n\n1. Open a business bank account using the permit number\n2. Register for VAT once turnover exceeds the threshold (see the earlier tax-registration FCE)\n3. Submit your annual income statement by April 30\n\n## Appeals\n\nThis decision can be appealed within **30 days** of the effective date. To appeal, open a new dialog with the trade register service desk."
    },
    "decision-doc-tx": {
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# DECISION — Business permit\n\n**Permit number** BP-2026-77231\n**Case reference** REF-2026-3142\n**Decision date** 2026-06-13\n**Effective from** 2026-06-15\n\n## Granted\n\nThe trade register hereby grants a business permit under the terms applied for. The permit is unconditional and does not require periodic renewal as long as the entity remains in good standing.\n\n## Conditions\n\n- Annual filing obligations as set out in the registration confirmation\n- Notification of any change in registered address within 30 days\n- VAT registration triggered automatically at turnover threshold\n\n## Appeals\n\n30 days from the effective date. Address: Appeals committee, trade register.\n\n*This is a fictional decision generated by the dialogporten-serviceprovider playbook demo.*"
    }
  }
}